\section*{AQFT Locality of Unitary Vertex Operator Algebras}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a mathematical result relevant to this question in the selected manuscript. Simple strongly rational unitary VOAs are claimed to generate completely rational nets, with unitary modules and a braided unitary equivalence to finite-index sectors.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Energy bounds establish strong locality of the generating fields. Annular charged-field estimates integrate modules, positive fusion forms give unitary tensor structure, and rationality identifies net sectors; the cited extension theorems then relate local net extensions to conformal VOA extensions.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The strong-locality result assumes simple unitary strong rationality. The problem statement asks locality for every unitary VOA without that rationality hypothesis. This entry records partial support; complete coverage of the question is not established by this catalogue.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 280, the documented entry establishes energy bounds, strong locality, and an irreducible conformal-net construction. Complete rationality, unitary module classification, tensor equivalence, and extension classification are omitted. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{VertexAlgebraNet.lean}. The inventory does not supply a named declaration for these Comparator entries. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

